
 ChangeLog for LAME
-==================-

 - All dates/times are in GMT.
 - Generated from svn log entries (svn2cl)

-- 

2026-11-05 11:12  aleidinger

	* maintainer/check-dist.ps1, maintainer/check-dist.sh:
	  Count the patch level of a release in the distribution check

2026-11-05 11:12  aleidinger

	* doc/maintainer-check-dist.md, maintainer/check-dist.ps1:
	  Pass the library folders and platforms from check-dist.ps1 to the
	  matrix
	  
	  The tarball carries none of the optional libraries, so the
	  Windows check
	  skipped the decoder, libsndfile and DirectShow cells whatever was
	  installed.

2026-11-05 11:11  aleidinger

	* doc/maintainer-build-matrix.md, maintainer/gen-build-matrix.ps1:
	  Honour the library folders in every Windows matrix cell
	  
	  The folders given to the matrix reached only the nmake cells; the
	  MSBuild and
	  client cells looked under vc_solution regardless. The mpg123 and
	  libsndfile
	  options now name a folder with one subfolder per platform, as the
	  setup script
	  lays them out, and each cell gets the path for its platform.

2026-11-05 11:11  aleidinger

	* maintainer/check-optdoc.py:
	  Read the long options from the parser as it is written now
	  
	  The check still looked for the macros that the parser lost when
	  it was split
	  into one function per group, so it found no option at all and
	  failed.

2026-11-05 11:11  aleidinger

	* doc/man/lame.1:
	  Document --athaa-sensitivity in the manual page

2026-11-05 11:11  aleidinger

	* doc/maintainer-gen-usage.md:
	  Name usage.html as the source of the examples in USAGE

2026-11-05 11:10  aleidinger

	* USAGE, doc/html/usage.html, maintainer/gen-usage.py:
	  Number the notes in the generated USAGE
	  
	  The generator printed the notes as bullets, so nothing matched
	  the [1] and
	  [2] in the text, and a hand edit had added them a second time. It
	  now numbers
	  them under a Notes heading, separates table columns and keeps the
	  text in
	  front of a table. USAGE is generated again, with the option
	  descriptions that
	  changed since the hand edit.

2026-11-01 20:48  aleidinger

	* test/unit/test_gain_analysis.c:
	  Compare title gains by histogram step in the ReplayGain test
	  
	  The test compared the title gain with its reference for exact
	  equality. On
	  32-bit x86 without SSE, both lie on the same histogram step, but
	  the
	  reference keeps more precision than a float, so the test failed.
	  A gain now
	  fails when it is half a step or more from the reference.

2026-11-01 20:47  aleidinger

	* test/unit/test_quantize_lines_vector.c:
	  Give the SSE control register accesses of a vector test the SSE
	  attribute
	  
	  The quantization vector test reads and sets MXCSR itself. On
	  32-bit x86, where
	  the compiler does not enable SSE by default, it did not compile,
	  and make
	  check stopped before any test ran. The two accesses now sit in
	  functions
	  marked like the library's own SSE code.

2026-11-01 20:47  aleidinger

	* doc/maintainer-build-matrix.md, maintainer/gen-build-matrix.sh:
	  Build the internal options in a matrix cell of their own
	  
	  The debug cell enabled the internal options, which configure
	  accepts only in
	  an alpha version. So the distribution check of a beta or a
	  release tarball
	  failed in that cell. The internal options now have their own
	  cell, and the
	  matrix skips it outside an alpha.

2026-11-01 20:47  aleidinger

	* include/lame.h, libmp3lame/lame.c, libmp3lame/set_get.c:
	  Return -2 for every failed allocation in an encode call
	  
	  An encode call returned -10 when the resampler could not allocate
	  its
	  buffers, and -2 when any other allocation failed. The
	  documentation of the
	  encode and flush functions now lists each return value as a
	  number.

2026-11-01 20:47  aleidinger

	* doc/doxygen/vector-dispatch.dox:
	  Remove project-internal notes from the vector dispatch page
	  
	  The page named the CPU of a test machine and listed lessons from
	  how an
	  experiment was run. Neither describes the code.

