	  Redesign the settings of the ACM codec and the DirectShow filter
	  
	  The ACM codec offers CBR, ABR and VBR formats, each family with
	  its own
	  range. Its settings dialog has two tabs, Formats and Encoding,
	  and adds
	  the encoding quality, VBR bitrate limits and the advanced
	  settings of
	  the filter.
	  
	  The DirectShow filter drops voice mode, no short blocks and mode
	  fixed,
	  and adds the private bit, the bit reservoir and ABR, also through
	  the
	  new IAudioEncoderProperties2 interface.
	  
	  Both use the desktop font, the same names and texts for the same
	  settings, and the same About box.

