	* USAGE, doc/html/detailed.html, doc/man/lame.1,
	  libmp3lame/gain_analysis.c, libmp3lame/gain_analysis.h,
	  maintainer/gen-usage.py:
	  Replace the dead replaygain.org reference in the ReplayGain
	  documentation
	  
	  The manual page, the HTML documentation and the gain_analysis
	  headers sent
	  readers to www.replaygain.org for what ReplayGain is and how the
	  gain is
	  computed. That domain has served unrelated content since at least
	  2017
	  (Debian bug #859636). The specification is kept on the
	  Hydrogenaudio wiki
	  now, and the page there describes the algorithm libmp3lame
	  implements, down
	  to the filter coefficients.
	  
	  What ReplayGain is, how LAME measures it and where the value goes
	  is said
	  once: in a REPLAYGAIN section of the manual page, and as the
	  introduction
	  of a ReplayGain group in the HTML documentation, each giving the
	  specification's address. The option entries say what each switch
	  changes
	  and point there. gen-usage.py no longer breaks a word longer than
	  the line
	  width, which the address is.

