	* doc/html/history.html, dshow/Mpegac.cpp,
	  test/clients/dshow_test.cpp:
	  Answer the DirectShow encoder's capability list without crashing
	  
	  IAMStreamConfig::GetStreamCaps() describes what the encoder can
	  produce, and
	  it built each answer by copying the output pin's own media type
	  and writing
	  an MP3 format into the copy. That type carries no format block
	  before the pin
	  connects, which is the state an application enumerating formats
	  finds it in,
	  and none afterwards either when the pin has connected as a stream
	  - which is
	  what a file writer downstream asks for. In both cases the write
	  went through
	  a null pointer and the application taking inventory of the
	  encoder crashed.
	  
	  The entry is now built from the capability table, so what the pin
	  happens to
	  be connected as no longer decides whether the call works.
	  
	  The index one past the last entry was accepted as well. It read
	  the zeroed
	  slot after the table and divided by its 0 Hz sample rate; it is
	  refused now,
	  as is the same index on the side that fills the table in, where
	  the bound was
	  tested after the store rather than before it.
	  
	  The filter-graph test asks for the capability list in both pin
	  states, and
	  for the boundary indices. Reported by an anonymous user, bug
	  ticket #424.

