	* doc/html/history.html, dshow/Mpegac.cpp,
	  test/clients/dshow_test.cpp:
	  Query the DirectShow output pin's own parent class
	  
	  The encoder's output pin is built on CTransformOutputPin, and its
	  interface
	  query handed anything it did not recognise to CBaseOutputPin
	  instead - the
	  class below that. What CTransformOutputPin answers for itself is
	  seeking:
	  it passes IMediaSeeking and IMediaPosition back to whatever feeds
	  the
	  filter's input, so that an application can ask the graph how long
	  the stream
	  is and where it is. Skipping it, the pin answered E_NOINTERFACE
	  and a graph
	  containing the filter could not be seeked.
	  
	  The filter object's own query already goes to its direct parent;
	  this makes
	  the pin agree with it.
	  
	  The filter-graph test gains the arm that distinguishes the two:
	  with the
	  input pin connected, the output pin is asked for both interfaces
	  and for the
	  duration of the stream. Asking for the duration as well is what
	  separates a
	  pin that answers the question from one that also knows the
	  answer.

