	  Declare libmp3lame's private link dependencies in lame.pc
	  
	  Linking a program against a static libmp3lame through pkg-config
	  yields
	  only -lmp3lame. lame.pc names no private dependencies, so the
	  math
	  library is unresolved in every build, and libmpg123 as well
	  wherever the
	  decoder is configured in.
	  
	  Name them from the same configure decisions the library is built
	  with.
	  libmpg123 goes in Requires.private, which also brings its search
	  path and
	  its own private libraries; the math library has no pkg-config
	  file of its
	  own, so it goes in Libs.private, as whichever library configure
	  selected.
	  
	  Only what libmp3lame itself links is named. The command line
	  tools use
	  several further libraries, and none of them belongs in a file
	  that
	  describes the library.
	  
	  A unit test compares the file with libtool's record of the link
	  in both
	  directions, so it can neither fall behind what the library needs
	  nor
	  offer a consumer more than it does.
	  
