	* libmp3lame/psymodel.c, libmp3lame/psymodel.h:
	  Document the psychoacoustic model
	  
	  The model carried no reference documentation, and the account in
	  its file
	  header no longer matched the encoder: it described two tonality
	  estimators
	  where there is one, an optional additive-masking mode that is not
	  optional,
	  and an unpredictability term that no longer exists.
	  
	  That header is replaced with a description of what the model
	  computes and in
	  what order, and every function and tuning constant gains one. Two
	  constants
	  are described as reachable only from disabled code, because that
	  is what they
	  are; the pre-echo control they belong to now runs after the
	  mapping to
	  scalefactor bands, where the position of an attack inside the
	  granule is
	  known.

2026-08-16 17:48  aleidinger

	* frontend/rtp.c:
	  Declare the RTP header's bit-fields unsigned
	  
	  The RTP version is 2 and the header's version field is two bits
	  wide, but the
	  field was declared signed, so the value does not fit and a
	  compiler that
	  rejects a truncation which changes a constant stops the build
	  outright. The
	  sequence number has the same shape: sixteen bits, seeded from a
	  random value
	  that uses all of them, and read back negative ever since.
	  
	  Nothing about the packets changes. The header goes on the wire by
	  casting the
	  structure to four words and putting each into network byte order,
	  so what is
	  sent is the bit pattern rather than the value, and that pattern
	  is the same
	  under either declaration - as the unit test covering the emitted
	  packets
	  asserts, version and payload type and an advancing sequence
	  number included.

