	  opened at all from an unpacked release. Working copies were
	  unaffected.

2026-08-16 10:36  aleidinger

	* ACM/AEncodeProperties.cpp, test/clients/acm_test.cpp:
	  Give the ACM codec a save that works without a file to start from
	  
	  Loading a configuration and saving one were not the same shape.
	  The load
	  side is a public method the driver calls when it is created. The
	  save side
	  was a method with an empty body next to a writer that required
	  the
	  configuration file to already exist and to already be well
	  formed: it read
	  the file, and returned having written nothing when that read
	  failed.
	  
	  The installer lays a configuration file down beside the codec, so
	  this
	  normally holds. When it does not - the file removed, emptied or
	  damaged -
	  the settings dialog appeared to work and nothing was kept, with
	  nothing said
	  about it, and the next load went back to the defaults.
	  
	  The writer now builds the elements it needs when they are not
	  there, so a
	  save succeeds against a missing or empty file, and the empty
	  method is the
	  counterpart its name promised: it writes the parameters the
	  object holds to
	  the configuration it was loaded from. The dialog saves through
	  it.
	  
	  Loading still writes nothing when there is no file to read. The
	  defaults
	  stand until something asks for a save, rather than every instance
	  of a driver
	  writing into the directory the codec was installed into, for a
	  change the
	  user did not make.
	  
	  Also here, in the same function: a configuration entry carrying
	  no name was
	  asked to compare its name, and the file is edited by hand often
	  enough for
	  that to matter.

