	* test/Makefile.am, test/Makefile.in, test/clients/acm_test.cpp,
	  test/clients/mp3frame.h, vc_solution/vs_lame_acm_test.vcxproj:
	  Drive the ACM codec through the Audio Compression Manager in its
	  test
	  
	  The rate and configuration checks compile the codec's sources in,
	  which says
	  nothing about the codec Windows actually loads. This adds a
	  second part that
	  takes the built binary and hands it to the ACM: the framework
	  registers the
	  driver for the calling process alone - no registry entry, no
	  administrator -
	  and then does the message dispatch, the format negotiation and
	  the buffer
	  handling, as an application converting audio would.
	  
	  A second of a sine wave is encoded and the result is read back as
	  MPEG frames
	  rather than counted as bytes. A byte total that comes out low
	  cannot
	  distinguish a tail the encoder never flushed from a bitrate it
	  quietly
	  substituted; the frame headers can.

