	* dshow/UIDS.H:
	  Make the DirectShow filter's GUID comments agree with its GUIDs
	  
	  Each identifier is written twice: once as the registry spelling
	  in a comment
	  and once as the numbers the compiler reads. All four disagreed,
	  every one of
	  them in the second field, and nothing in a build compares the
	  two.
	  
	  The numbers are what the filter registers and instantiates under,
	  so the
	  comments are what changes. They are also the form a reader copies
	  into a
	  registry entry or a bug report, where the wrong value points at a
	  class that
	  does not exist.

