	* frontend/parse.c, libmp3lame/id3tag.c, misc/abx.c:
	  Convert to unsigned char before calling the character class
	  functions
	  
	  The <ctype.h> functions are defined for the values of an unsigned
	  char
	  and for EOF, and nothing else. The seventeen call sites that
	  passed a
	  plain char directly could reach them with a negative value for
	  any byte
	  above 0x7F - on glibc, an index taken from before the start of
	  the
	  classification table. Ordinary input reaches them: a tag field or
	  a
	  genre name with an accented letter, and a command line with one.
	  
	  The two ID3 helpers that need this in several places now say it
	  once.

2026-08-16 10:25  aleidinger

	* libmp3lame/takehiro.c:
	  Bound the previous-noise lookup to the scale factor bands that
	  exist
	  
	  When the upper part of a granule is zero the quantization loop
	  skips the
	  remaining bands by setting the band index one past the last one.
	  The
	  previous-noise cache is still consulted at that index in the same
	  pass,
	  and for a short block that index is one past the end of the cache
	  array,
	  so the branch it decides was taken on whatever followed the array
	  in
	  memory rather than on a noise value. Restrict the lookup to
	  indices the
	  cache has.
	  
	  The assertion a few functions further down stated only the upper
	  half of
	  the range its two reads need; it now states both.

2026-08-09 17:56  aleidinger

	* Makefile.MSVC, doc/doxygen/vector-dispatch.dox,
	  libmp3lame/lame.c, libmp3lame/takehiro.c, libmp3lame/util.c,
	  libmp3lame/util.h, libmp3lame/vbrquantize.c,
	  libmp3lame/vector/Makefile.am, libmp3lame/vector/Makefile.in,
	  libmp3lame/vector/avx512_calc_sfb_noise.c,
	  libmp3lame/vector/avx512_choose_table.c,
	  libmp3lame/vector/lame_intrin.h, test/unit/Makefile.am,
	  test/unit/Makefile.in, test/unit/test_calc_sfb_noise_vector.c,
	  test/unit/test_choose_table_vector.c,
	  vc_solution/vs_libmp3lame.vcxproj,
	  vc_solution/vs_libmp3lame.vcxproj.filters:
	  Drop the two AVX-512 routines the measurements did not support
	  
	  Two vector routines were carried unreachable, behind environment
	  variables and
	  an alpha-only build, so that the one thing nobody could answer
	  from a desk
	  could be answered from a machine: what they cost inside a real
	  encode. Testers
	  on two microarchitectures have now answered it, twenty-five runs
	  an arm in both
	  orderings, and neither routine earns its place.
	  
	  The scalefactor-band noise estimate costs about five percent of a
	  variable
	  bitrate encode where it runs at all, and cannot be told from zero
	  on the other
	  part. Its reduction is pinned to a fixed association so that
	  every processor of
	  an architecture produces the same bits, and that pin does not
	  widen with the
	  registers, so the extra lanes buy the cost of entering them and
	  nothing else.
	  
	  The Huffman table search splits by vendor, a small gain on one
	  and a cost on
	  the other, and it is reached from both the constant and the
	  variable bitrate
	  paths - so there is no setting at which it could be turned on for
	  everyone
	  without the mode test the dispatch ladder exists to avoid.
	  
	  The tier above AVX2 keeps the routine that did earn it, the
	  quantization loop.
	  Nothing a user can observe changes: no released version compiled
	  either of the
	  removed routines, and no build ran them unless its environment
	  asked.
	  
	  The reasoning, the numbers and what they were measured against
	  are in the
	  internal dispatch documentation, next to the older decisions of
	  the same shape,
	  because a routine that was written and then rejected is exactly
	  the work that
	  gets done twice if the result is not written down.

