	* doc/html/history.html, frontend/get_audio.c,
	  test/unit/test_get_audio_wav.c:
	  Refuse a WAVE sample width the reader cannot unpack
	  
	  The WAVE reader guarded only against a width of zero, so any
	  other value the
	  header declared was taken at face value. Integer widths it has no
	  case for were
	  caught later, by the sample reader, in a message naming neither
	  the file nor the
	  field.
	  
	  Floating point data was worse off. Such a file is read at 32 bits
	  and converted;
	  declared at any other width it was unpacked as integers of that
	  width and the
	  buffer then reinterpreted as floats, which produced noise and no
	  diagnostic
	  anywhere along the way.
	  
	  The accepted widths are now settled where the header is read,
	  from what the
	  reader implements: 8, 16, 24 and 32 bit integers, and 32 bit
	  floating point.
	  The AIFF reader has enumerated its widths all along; the two now
	  agree.

