	* libmp3lame/set_get.c:
	  Document what an input sample rate does and does not survive
	  
	  The reference described the resampling but not what becomes of
	  the input rate
	  itself. It is recorded nowhere in the stream: a frame names its
	  own sampling
	  frequency from the fixed set the format defines, so a decoder
	  reports the rate
	  LAME encoded at, and the rate the material arrived at cannot be
	  recovered from
	  the file.
	  
	  The accepted range is now stated as well. There is no upper bound
	  beyond the
	  parameter's own type, and rates far above anything the output
	  formats allow are
	  resampled like any other.

