	* frontend/get_audio.c, test/unit/Makefile.am,
	  test/unit/Makefile.in, test/unit/test_get_audio_wav.c:
	  Reject a WAVE sample rate the encoder cannot represent
	  
	  A WAVE header states its sample rate in 32 unsigned bits, while
	  the encoder
	  takes that rate as a signed integer. A file declaring a rate in
	  the upper half
	  of the field's range was converted before anything examined it,
	  and the refusal
	  that followed reported the converted value - a header claiming
	  4294967295 Hz
	  was refused as a sample rate of -1, a number appearing nowhere in
	  the file.
	  
	  The rate is now checked while the declared value is still intact,
	  so such a
	  header is refused as the malformed field it is and the message
	  names the rate
	  the file actually carries. Nothing the encoder can use is
	  affected: the high
	  rates it resamples down are accepted as before, and the accepted
	  range now ends
	  exactly where the encoder's own does.
	  
	  The AIFF reader already checks its sample rate this way; the two
	  readers now
	  agree.

