	* doc/doxygen/vector-dispatch.dox, libmp3lame/util.c:
	  Read the AVX-512 experiment switches once per encode
	  
	  The two environment variables that select the experimental
	  AVX-512 kernels were
	  read wherever the question was asked. One of those places is the
	  dispatch of the
	  scalefactor-band noise estimate, which a variable-bitrate encode
	  enters millions
	  of times, so a machine running the AVX-512 tier walked the whole
	  environment
	  block on each of them - and did so precisely when the variable
	  was unset, which
	  is the arm anyone measuring the experiment uses as their
	  reference.
	  
	  The cost is large enough to be mistaken for the thing under test.
	  It appears
	  only on that tier and only in variable-bitrate mode, because
	  those are the
	  conditions the gate tests, so it wears the shape of a processor's
	  behaviour;
	  two testers on different vendors reported it as one, and it
	  reproduces on a
	  machine that cannot execute a single AVX-512 instruction.
	  
	  The environment is now read where the vector routines are chosen,
	  once, as the
	  encoder is initialised. Both switches are settings of a run
	  rather than
	  questions asked inside it, so setting either after initialisation
	  no longer has
	  an effect - which is what a switch this shape should have meant
	  all along.
	  
	  Nothing a released build does changes: the whole path is compiled
	  only into an
	  alpha, and the value returned for any given environment is the
	  same one as
	  before.

