	  Skip the strict cell where its automake is absent, rather than
	  failing
	  
	  The build matrix has one cell that enables maintainer mode, and
	  maintainer mode
	  switches on the Autotools rebuild rules. Those call the
	  version-suffixed tool
	  the generated Makefiles name, so on a machine carrying a
	  different automake the
	  tool is simply not there, make stops with status 127, and the
	  distribution check
	  reports a failure that is about the host rather than about the
	  source.
	  
