	  own configure and
	  treats it like any other missing prerequisite: the cell is not
	  laid out, and
	  matrix-info.txt records why. Nothing has to be kept in step by
	  hand when the
	  tree is regenerated with a newer automake.
	  
	  A cell that is not laid out had no directory and so left no trace
	  in the
	  distribution check at all - the run merely had fewer checks in
	  it, with nothing
	  saying which were gone. Each one is now reported as a skipped
	  check naming its
	  reason, which also covers the cells dropped for a missing
	  library. A
	  configuration that quietly stops being checked is worse than one
	  that says it is
	  not being checked.

