2026-08-01 09:11  aleidinger

	* Makefile.MSVC, maintainer/gen-build-matrix.ps1,
	  vc_solution/README.vs.txt, vc_solution/vs_libmpg123_config.props,
	  vc_solution/vs_libsndfile_config.props:
	  Build each project's mpg123 import library separately
	  
	  The Windows distribution of libmpg123 ships a module definition
	  file and no
	  import library, so the build makes one. It made it in the
	  distribution folder,
	  from a property sheet that every project using the decoder
	  shares, and those
	  projects are built in parallel - so on a folder nobody had built
	  in yet they all
	  wrote that one file at the same moment, and the build failed on
	  whichever
	  project lost. The library then stayed behind in a directory the
	  build does not
	  own, and the nmake build had quietly come to depend on finding it
	  there.
	  
	  Each project now builds its own into its own intermediate
	  directory, and the
	  nmake build into its output directory. Nothing is written into
	  the distribution
	  folder any more, which needs only the headers, the definition
	  file and the DLL.
	  
	  The runtime libraries copied next to the binaries are shared in
	  the same way, so
	  those copies now leave a file that is already in place alone.

2026-08-01 08:36  aleidinger

	* doc/html/history.html, libmp3lame/id3tag.c,
	  test/unit/test_id3tag.c:
	  Keep ID3v2 frames whose descriptions differ apart
	  
	  Frames identified by a description - TXXX, WXXX and COMM - were
	  taken to be
	  the same frame whenever the stored description merely began the
	  incoming one,
	  so the second of --tv "TXXX=foo=..." and --tv "TXXX=foobar=..."
	  replaced the
	  first and its text was lost. An empty description begins every
	  other one, so a
	  comment carrying none vanished as soon as a described comment was
	  added.
	  
	  A description now has to end where the stored one does. Repeating
	  a
	  description still replaces the frame it names, so correcting a
	  value is
	  unaffected.

2026-08-01 08:35  aleidinger

	* doc/html/history.html, frontend/get_audio.c,
	  maintainer/coverage-workload.txt:
	  Read a file as headerless PCM only when that was asked for
	  
	  A build configured to hand file input to libsndfile accepted
	  anything: when
	  libsndfile did not recognise a file, it was retried as raw PCM at
	  the
	  default rate and channel count, so a corrupt or wrong-format file
	  - eight
	  bytes of anything at all - encoded to a valid MP3 of noise and
	  reported
	  success. The same files are refused by a build using LAME's own
	  reader,
	  which decided long ago that failing beats encoding hundreds of
	  formats it
	  does not support.
	  
	  The retry now happens only for input the user marked as raw with
	  -r, which
	  is the only thing that can say so: libsndfile cannot recognise
	  headerless
	  PCM, so an unrecognised file is nothing more than unrecognised.
	  Everything
	  else falls through to LAME's reader and is refused there.

