	* config.h.in, configMS.h, configure, configure.ac,
	  frontend/parse.c, libmp3lame/bitstream.c, libmp3lame/lame.c,
	  libmp3lame/set_get.c, libmp3lame/util.c,
	  maintainer/gen-coverage-matrix.sh, test/unit/test_set_get.c:
	  Use one name for the condition that the decoder is built in
	  
	  Two macros were defined together and meant the same thing:
	  HAVE_MPG123,
	  saying libmpg123 is present, and DECODE_ON_THE_FLY, naming the
	  feature that
	  needs it. The Windows configuration header derived the second
	  from the
	  first, so no build system here could set one without the other,
	  and a
	  reader had no way to tell that from two genuinely independent
	  conditions.
	  
	  DECODE_ON_THE_FLY is the one that goes. An out-of-tree build
	  system that
	  defines it has to define HAVE_MPG123 instead - otherwise the code
	  that
	  decodes while encoding is quietly compiled out rather than
	  failing to
	  build.

