	* doc/maintainer-build-matrix.md, maintainer/gen-build-matrix.sh:
	  Add a matrix cell that builds without the decoder under fatal
	  warnings
	  
	  The matrix is a star, one cell per configuration axis, which
	  assumes that a
	  regression in an axis is visible from that axis alone. That does
	  not hold
	  where one surface is reachable only through another: the code
	  compiled when
	  the decoder is absent is compiled nowhere else, so an ordinary
	  build has
	  nothing to warn about, and the decoder-off cell does not make a
	  warning
	  fatal. Both flips are needed before there is anything to see,
	  which is why
	  the failures this covers were each found by hand instead.
	  
	  The unit tests stay out of the cell list on purpose. The existing
	  option for
	  extra configure arguments adds them to every cell, this one
	  included, which
	  is the wider combination for no extra cells.

