	* maintainer/abi/libmp3lame.abi:
	  Refresh the ABI baseline after the vector-routines work
	  
	  Adding the vector-routines interface and retiring the MMX and
	  3DNow! enables
	  changed both the set of exported entry points and the layout of
	  the state
	  behind them. Both were intended; what was missed is that the
	  baseline the ABI
	  check compares against still describes the state before them, so
	  the check
	  reports a change that nobody has recorded a decision about.
	  
	  Record it. The interface only gained entry points, and every
	  layout change
	  reported is inside structures a caller reaches solely through an
	  opaque
	  handle, so nothing that links today stops linking and the soname
	  stands.

