	* doc/html/history.html, include/lame.def, include/lame.h,
	  include/libmp3lame.sym, libmp3lame/set_get.c,
	  maintainer/abi/libmp3lame.abi, test/unit/test_set_get.c:
	  Add lame_get_asm_optimizations()
	  
	  lame_set_asm_optimizations() allows or forbids an instruction-set
	  family, and
	  nothing could read that setting back: neither what a preset or
	  another part of
	  a program had left behind, nor whether a family a caller named
	  was one this
	  library knows. The setter cannot answer the second question at
	  all - it accepts
	  an unrecognized family, sets nothing, and returns the value it
	  was given, which
	  is indistinguishable from success.
	  
	  The new getter answers for one family at a time, the same shape
	  the setter
	  takes, and distinguishes four answers: the family is allowed, it
	  has been
	  forbidden, the instance is not usable, or the family is not
	  available in this
	  instance. It reports the setting rather than the instruction set
	  an encode will
	  really use: the families are not independent, so forbidding SSE
	  also rules out
	  AVX2 while the AVX2 setting stays as it was.
	  
	  This adds an exported symbol and the ABI baseline records it. No
	  existing
	  behaviour changes, and no soname bump is needed for an addition.

