	  vc_solution/vs_lame_mp3x.vcxproj.filters:
	  build: retire the GTK 1.2 frame analyzer
	  
	  The frame analyzer is a GTK 4 program now. Its GTK 1.2
	  predecessor was still
	  in the tree and still shipped in the release archive while being
	  compiled
	  nowhere, and the build system and the build notes went on
	  describing how to
	  obtain and link GTK 1.2 on three platforms. None of it is
	  reachable any more,
	  so the sources, the build support and the notes go together
	  rather than
	  documenting something that is not there.
	  
	  On Windows the analyzer is a Visual Studio target, built for x64
	  alone: GTK 4
	  for MSVC is published for that architecture and for no other, so
	  a 32-bit
	  analyzer would have nothing to link against. That also takes it
	  out of the
	  nmake makefile, whose native target is 32-bit x86; the makefile
	  names where to
	  build it instead. The Visual Studio project finds GTK 4 the same
	  way it finds
	  mpg123 and libsndfile - a per-platform folder under vc_solution -
	  rather than
	  at a fixed path on a fixed drive.
	  
	  On the autotools side the bundled macro that located GTK 1.2
	  through the
	  obsolete gtk-config script has no caller left, so it goes, and
	  with it the
	  three configure options that came with it - --with-gtk-prefix,
	  --with-gtk-exec-prefix and --disable-gtktest - which described a
	  search that
	  no longer happens and would have gone on being offered in
	  configure --help.
	  The coverage harness was probing for that same gtk-config script
	  to decide
	  whether the analyzer could be covered, so it was answering a
	  question nothing
	  asks any more; it now asks pkg-config for the GTK 4 that
	  configure requires.

