	  part of
	  the interface, because they carry a documentation comment and the
	  public
	  configuration could only filter out undocumented ones. They are
	  now
	  marked internal, like the internal functions around them.
	  
	  The development harnesses get their own place in the internal set
	  rather
	  than being scattered through the page list, with a short parent
	  page
	  explaining what each is for.

2026-07-27 14:57  aleidinger

	* configure, configure.ac:
	  configure: skip the PIE frontend flags when there is no shared
	  library
	  
	  The default hardening builds the command line tools as
	  position-independent executables. That needs position-independent
	  objects to link against: it works when the tools link the shared
	  library, and cannot work when they link the static one, whose
	  objects
	  are not built PIC.
	  
	  The guard only recognised --disable-dynamic-frontends, which asks
	  for a
	  statically linked frontend explicitly. Configuring
	  --disable-shared
	  arrives at the same place implicitly - there is no shared library
	  left
	  for the tools to link - and they were still asked to be
	  position-independent. On a toolchain that does not default to PIE
	  that
	  combination fails to link. Skip the flags in both cases.

