	  doc: document the input-stream parameters for the public API
	  reference
	  
	  Continues filling in the public API documentation with the
	  settings that
	  describe the encoder's input: how many samples there are, at what
	  rate
	  and in how many channels, what to scale them by, and what rate to
	  write
	  into the stream.
	  
	  Two properties of this whole interface are stated once, at the
	  file, and
	  not repeated on every function. A setter validates only what it
	  can see,
	  so whether a combination of settings is usable is decided later;
	  and a
	  getter cannot report an error at all - given an unusable instance
	  it
	  returns 0, which for most of these settings is also a legitimate
	  value,
	  so a caller has to check the instance rather than the result.
	  
