	  read.
	  Both settings that describe the input have defaults, so an
	  encoder that
	  is never told about its input initializes successfully and
	  encodes as
	  though it were CD audio - a wrong result rather than an error.
	  And the
	  sample count is not a limit on encoding: it feeds a frame
	  estimate, and
	  its default is the documented "length not known" value rather
	  than a
	  count.
	  
