	* doc/Doxyfile-common.in, doc/Doxyfile-internal.in,
	  doc/Makefile.am, doc/Makefile.in:
	  doc: give the Doxygen templates a placeholder configure will not
	  consume
	  
	  The rule that expands the Doxyfile templates substituted a
	  placeholder
	  named the same as one of Autoconf's own variables. Because the
	  makefile
	  itself goes through config.status, the search pattern was
	  replaced along
	  with everything else, leaving a rule that looked for the absolute
	  source
	  path inside the template and matched nothing.
	  
	  Nothing was substituted, so both configurations were handed input
	  paths
	  that do not exist and documented an empty tree: the generated
	  output was
	  stylesheets and icons with not one page of content in it. Doxygen
	  reports
	  missing inputs as warnings among its others and still exits
	  successfully,
	  which is why the documentation appeared to build for as long as
	  it did.
	  
	  Renaming the placeholder to one Autoconf has no reason to touch
	  fixes it.
	  The neighbouring placeholders were never affected, having names
	  it does
	  not recognize. The internal configuration now produces 849 files
	  where it
	  produced 45, and the public one 152.

