	* configMS.h:
	  Let the configuration header report the standard header, not
	  include it
	  
	  A configuration header states what the platform has; including a
	  system
	  header from it puts that header in front of every translation
	  unit
	  whether or not it needs one. The sources that use the fixed-width
	  integer types already ask for them through the guard the rest of
	  the
	  tree uses, so reporting the header as present is enough to reach
	  them on
	  Windows too.

