2026-07-23 08:14  aleidinger

	* frontend/mp3rtp.c:
	  mp3rtp: stop truncating the destination address
	  
	  Where LAME is built without IPv6, the destination address is read
	  with a
	  field width of eleven characters into a buffer of sixteen. A
	  dotted quad can
	  be fifteen, so anything longer is silently cut short and the
	  stream is sent to
	  a different host than the one asked for, with no diagnostic -
	  including the
	  multicast address the program's own usage text suggests. Widen
	  the field to
	  what the buffer holds.

