	* INSTALL, doc/html/detailed.html, doc/man/lame.1, lame.spec.in:
	  Update the documentation for the vector code
	  
	  The manual page, the HTML option reference and the install notes
	  all described
	  the vectorized routines as assembler optimizations that appear
	  only if an
	  assembler was found at build time. Neither half is true any more:
	  the routines
	  are compiled into every x86 binary and chosen per processor at
	  run time, and
	  nothing needs an assembler.
	  
	  "--noasm" keeps its three values, but only one of them still
	  selects
	  something, so say which. The install notes also told readers to
	  build with a
	  makefile that was removed along with the bundled decoder.

