2026-07-19 15:23  aleidinger

	* configure, configure.ac:
	  Enable stricter warnings in maintainer mode
	  
	  When maintainer mode is configured, build the GCC/Clang tree with
	  -Wextra
	  and -Wshadow and treat all warnings as errors, so a lapse in
	  warning
	  cleanliness fails the build for developers. Regular and release
	  builds
	  are unaffected: maintainer mode is off by default, and each flag
	  is
	  probed for acceptance before use so an unsupported compiler skips
	  it.

2026-07-19 15:22  aleidinger

	* frontend/get_audio.c:
	  Use or drop the header fields the readers only skipped over
	  
	  Several WAV and AIFF header fields were parsed and then
	  discarded, and
	  two AIFF format identifiers were never referenced at all.
	  
	  Put the ones that carry a real invariant to work: an extensible
	  format
	  header now has to describe a large enough extension and may not
	  claim
	  more valid bits than its samples hold, and an AIFF file in 64 bit
	  floating point is named as unsupported instead of failing as if
	  it were
	  corrupt. The block alignment and byte rate only restate what the
	  other
	  fields say and are frequently written wrong, so they are reported
	  as a
	  mismatch under --verbose rather than rejected. The channel mask
	  is
	  advisory and is skipped, and the unreferenced identifier is
	  dropped.
	  
	  Well-formed files, including extensible ones, are unaffected.

2026-07-19 15:17  aleidinger

	* frontend/get_audio.c:
	  Detect and reject truncated WAV and AIFF headers
	  
	  The fixed-width byte readers used by the WAV and AIFF header
	  parsers
	  ignored the result of fread(), so a file ending in the middle of
	  a
	  header was parsed as if the missing bytes were zeros and could
	  drive the
	  encoder with bogus format parameters.
	  
	  Let the readers report a short read instead of returning a value
	  that
	  cannot be distinguished from data, and chain them at each call
	  site so
	  the first short read stops the remaining reads and rejects the
	  file
	  through the existing "corrupt or unsupported format" path.
	  Well-formed
	  files are unaffected.

2026-07-19 11:56  aleidinger

	* frontend/get_audio.c, libmp3lame/machine.h,
	  libmp3lame/mpglib_interface.c:
	  Mark intentionally-unused function parameters
	  
	  Several functions ignore some of their parameters: the
	  compatibility
	  decode entry points always fail, the analysis-hook setters are
	  not yet
	  implemented, and the MP3 reader and its file opener reach their
	  input
	  through global state or use their arguments only when the MPEG
	  decoder
	  is built in.
	  
	  Add a portable attribute macro for a deliberately-unused
	  parameter and
	  apply it at these sites. Because the attribute states that a
	  parameter
	  may go unused rather than that it does, it also covers the
	  arguments
	  that are live only in one of the two decoder configurations,
	  leaving a
	  build with extra parameter warnings quiet either way. The normal
	  build
	  is unaffected.

