2026-07-19 09:12  aleidinger

	* libmp3lame/psymodel.c:
	  Avoid an uninitialized read in the VBR block-type decision on
	  mono
	  
	  When encoding a single channel, the VBR block-type decision still
	  consults a two-channel long/short-block array whose second entry
	  is
	  never filled, so the channel-coupling test reads uninitialized
	  stack.
	  Depending on that value it could spuriously force short blocks on
	  a mono
	  frame.
	  
	  Initialize both entries to the neutral long-block value. The real
	  channels are overwritten by the attack detector, so stereo is
	  unaffected and the absent second channel no longer influences the
	  coupled decision. Encoder output is unchanged for well-formed
	  input.

2026-07-19 09:12  aleidinger

	* maintainer/gen-build-matrix.sh:
	  gen-build-matrix.sh: build each matrix cell in its own directory
	  
	  The generated per-cell build script and the driver both ran from
	  the
	  matrix master directory, so every cell configured and built there
	  rather
	  than in its own out-of-tree directory, each overwriting the
	  previous
	  cell's configuration and object files. The matrix therefore never
	  tested
	  the configurations in isolation: a cell's pass/fail and its build
	  warnings reflected whatever survived the last cell's clobbering.
	  
	  Have each generated build script change into its own directory
	  before
	  configuring, so every cell is a genuine isolated out-of-tree
	  build.

