	  which takes no length for the area it writes, so a terminal whose
	  capability string was longer than the buffer overran it. Pass a
	  null
	  area so the library returns the string from its own storage, and
	  copy
	  that out under the existing bound.

2026-07-17 18:12  aleidinger

	* libmp3lame/id3tag.c, test/unit/test_id3tag.c:
	  libmp3lame: refuse an ID3v2 tag too large for its size field
	  
	  The ID3v2 tag length is stored in a 28-bit synchsafe field. Album
	  art or
	  padding supplied by the caller can push the tag past that, at
	  which point
	  the four length bytes wrap and describe a shorter tag than was
	  written,
	  leaving the frames after it unparseable. Produce no tag in that
	  case
	  rather than a corrupt one.
	  
	  The unit tests drive the size over the limit through both the
	  padding and
	  the album-art paths and confirm an ordinary tag is still written.

