2026-07-17 12:45  aleidinger

	* libmp3lame/quantize.c:
	  libmp3lame: record the accepted quantization's own bit count as
	  the best
	  
	  The outer search loop filled its "best bit count" from the
	  incumbent one
	  statement before the accepted candidate replaced it, so the value
	  trailed the
	  search by one accepted candidate, while the adjacent noise
	  bookkeeping recorded
	  the correct one. The bound derived from it in the no-distortion
	  branch was
	  biased tight, because scalefactor amplification trends toward
	  more bits.
	  
	  Take the count from the candidate being accepted. VBR output is
	  unchanged; CBR
	  and ABR output changes, with no measurable difference in
	  perceived quality.

2026-07-17 12:45  aleidinger

	* libmp3lame/vbrquantize.c:
	  libmp3lame: keep VBR scalefactors above their minimum when
	  reducing bits
	  
	  When a granule runs out of bits the reduction step flattens the
	  scalefactor
	  distribution toward the global gain, but it bounded the result
	  only to the
	  representable range, not to each band's minimum scalefactor.
	  Under bit
	  starvation a band could then be handed a scalefactor below the
	  minimum the
	  allocator requires - the sibling reduction path already guards
	  against this.
	  Apply the same lower bound here, so every path that feeds the
	  allocator keeps
	  each band at or above its minimum.

2026-07-17 12:42  aleidinger

	* frontend/parse.c:
	  frontend: guard setlocale() the same way as its header include
	  
	  parse.c includes <locale.h> only when both HAVE_ICONV and
	  HAVE_LANGINFO_H
	  are defined, but the setlocale(LC_CTYPE, "") call was guarded on
	  HAVE_LANGINFO_H alone. A configuration with langinfo but without
	  iconv then
	  compiled the call with neither setlocale() nor LC_CTYPE declared,
	  which
	  breaks the frontend build (seen on macOS with a C23 default). The
	  call only
	  prepares nl_langinfo() for the iconv conversions, so require
	  iconv for it as
	  well, matching the include.

2026-07-17 12:42  aleidinger

	* libmp3lame/encoder.c:
	  libmp3lame: convert analyzer spectrum data to double when copying
	  it
	  
	  The frame analyzer's per-band spectrum buffer holds double
	  values, but the
	  encoder-side copy filled it from the encoder's FLOAT array with a
	  raw byte
	  copy, which reinterprets the bit patterns instead of converting
	  them. In the
	  usual build where FLOAT is float the analyzer's MDCT display
	  therefore showed
	  garbage. Copy element by element so the values are converted,
	  correct for
	  either width of FLOAT.

2026-07-17 12:41  aleidinger

	* libmp3lame/lame.c, libmp3lame/util.c, libmp3lame/util.h:
	  libmp3lame: check the resampler's buffer allocations
	  
	  The resampler allocated its FIR input and filter buffers without
	  checking
	  the result and then dereferenced them while precomputing the
	  filter
	  coefficients, turning an allocation failure into a crash. Check
	  the
	  allocations, release any partial allocation, and report the
	  failure to
	  the caller as out of memory.

