2026-07-16 14:31  aleidinger

	* Makefile.am, Makefile.in, doc/Doxyfile-internal.in,
	  doc/Makefile.am, doc/Makefile.in, doc/doxygen/internal.md,
	  doc/maintainer-quality.md, maintainer/quality-compare.py,
	  maintainer/setup-quality-corpus.sh:
	  Add a quality regression harness
	  
	  A change to the psycho acoustic model or the quantizer is meant
	  to alter the
	  output, so the bitstream check that guards everything else says
	  nothing about
	  whether it was an improvement. Judging that by ear does not
	  survive review
	  either.
	  
	  One script lays out reference audio from the EBU SQAM CD, which
	  is not
	  shipped: its licence covers testing but not clearly
	  redistribution, so it is
	  fetched by hand and pointed at. The other encodes that audio with
	  a baseline
	  and a candidate build, scores each against the original with
	  PEAQ, and reports
	  the difference per track. Per track rather than as a total,
	  because a
	  regression in one hard case disappears into a corpus average -
	  which is what
	  the transient tracks in the default selection are there to catch.
	  
	  The scorer is not part of any distribution and has to be built;
	  where it is
	  missing the script says so and where to get it. Its scores are a
	  relative
	  signal between two builds, not a measure of absolute quality: no
	  free PEAQ
	  implementation meets the conformance requirements.

