2026-07-16 14:27  aleidinger

	* Makefile.am, Makefile.in, doc/Doxyfile-internal.in,
	  doc/Makefile.am, doc/Makefile.in, doc/doxygen/internal.md,
	  doc/maintainer-build-matrix.md, doc/maintainer-perf.md,
	  maintainer/perf-compare.sh:
	  Add a script to compare the encoding speed of two builds
	  
	  Timing an encoder by hand invites two mistakes that quietly
	  produce a wrong
	  answer. With dynamic frontends the encoder in the build directory
	  is a
	  libtool wrapper, so a naive run times a shell start-up; its
	  executable, used
	  directly, binds to an installed libmp3lame where the host has one
	  and then
	  measures that library rather than the build being tested.
	  
	  The script takes a baseline and a candidate build matrix, runs
	  both encoders
	  over the same input, and reports the difference along with
	  whether the
	  measurement varied too much to mean anything. It compares the
	  bitstreams in
	  the same pass, because a speedup that changes the output is a bug
	  unless the
	  change was meant to.

