	* libmp3lame/lame.c:
	  Drop three unreachable bitrate index fallbacks
	  
	  Each of the three bitrate index lookups in lame_init_params()
	  runs on a value
	  FindNearestBitrate() has just taken from the bitrate table, and
	  then clamps the
	  index in case the lookup failed. It cannot fail: both functions
	  work on the same
	  table row, derive the MPEG version from the sample rate the same
	  way, and the
	  value is handed straight from one to the other. A sweep over
	  every version and
	  sample rate, for bitrates from -10000 to 10000 kbps, reaches no
	  clamp.

