	* doc/html/history.html, libmp3lame/quantize_pvt.c,
	  libmp3lame/quantize_pvt.h, libmp3lame/takehiro.c,
	  libmp3lame/vbrquantize.c:
	  Honor the --enable-ieeehack configure switch
	  
	  The Takehiro IEEE-754 rounding shortcut is opt-in and off by
	  default, but
	  the switch never took effect: the guards tested whether the
	  configure
	  macro was defined rather than its value, and the build always
	  defines it,
	  so the shortcut was always compiled in. Test the value instead,
	  so the
	  default build uses the portable rounding path as intended.
	  
	  The shortcut only speeds up float-to-int conversion on much older
	  CPUs
	  that lack a fast native conversion instruction; on current
	  hardware
	  disabling it is faster, and the default output changes slightly
	  (a
	  different rounding table). Measured on a Xeon X5675, encoding a
	  23.8 min
	  corpus (hyperfine, 1 warmup + 10 hot runs, CPU-pinned):
	  
	  CBR -b320: 40.23 +/- 0.50 s -> 37.25 +/- 0.59 s (1.08x faster)
	  VBR -V2: 30.48 +/- 0.44 s -> 27.76 +/- 0.31 s (1.10x faster)
	  
	  SF bug #521

