	  libmp3lame, frontend: guard unchecked allocations against OOM
	  
	  Several allocation sites in the library init path and the
	  frontend
	  dereferenced the result without checking it, turning an
	  allocation
	  failure into a crash rather than a clean error. The trigger is
	  out-of-memory, not attacker input - but the crash is avoidable.
	  
	  Check these allocations and fail gracefully: the library init
	  path
	  reports the failure to its caller; the frontend paths print an
	  error and
	  stop. Sites that already handle failure are left alone, as are
	  two whose
	  fix is more invasive (the resampler init and an input-buffer
	  realloc),
	  which are better handled on their own.

